DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Mr. Chairman, it's always followed the same principle.

3921
02:54:34,090 --> 02:54:36,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: It's on a need base and assessed by the social worker.

3922
02:54:36,090 --> 02:54:39,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We get referrals every day from everywhere.

3923
02:54:39,090 --> 02:54:43,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And it's really up to the frontline social services, the social workers,

3924
02:54:43,090 --> 02:54:47,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: to see if we were to say yes or no to a particular request.

3925
02:54:47,090 --> 02:54:52,090
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: So would it be safe to say that ngayon mas regulated na natin, hindi na po magagaya?

3926
02:54:52,090 --> 02:54:57,090
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: For example, as a matter of fact, doon po sa distrito ko, during the previous congress,

3927
02:54:57,090 --> 02:55:06,090
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: ang AICS pinang babayad po sa, pinang pe-payout yan sa mga nagpupunta doon sa mga pre-election rally, campaign.

3928
02:55:06,090 --> 02:55:13,090
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: In fact, naging leaflets pa nga po yan eh. Pre-filled up na yung form.

3929
02:55:13,090 --> 02:55:18,090
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: Nakalagay na lang yung pangalan ng beneficiary at yung date. Tapos binabahay-bahay.

3930
02:55:18,090 --> 02:55:25,090
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: So have we corrected that? Dahil yung AICS is a stopgap for individuals na talagang kailangan ng tulong.

3931
02:55:25,090 --> 02:55:35,090
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: And it should not be used that way. Dahil kawawa naman yung mga taong kailangan talagang matulungan na nangangailangan ng tulong.

3932
02:55:35,090 --> 02:55:40,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Mr. Chairman, we totally agree. And we have tightened the implementing guidelines.

3933
02:55:40,090 --> 02:55:46,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: May mga anti-EPAL, may mga CLARO na you can't use it for your own interest or your political gains.

3934
02:55:46,090 --> 02:55:51,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: It's now enshrined both in the GAAA and at the same time our guidelines.

3935
02:55:51,090 --> 02:55:54,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And we take these things seriously. Kakasuhan yung mga empleyado.

3936
02:55:54,090 --> 02:55:59,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Meron rin hong ganung provision sa loob ng aming administrative codes in the department.

3937
02:55:59,090 --> 02:56:08,090
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: Okay. Mr. Chairsec, as pinakita kanina ni Congressman Tino yung graph,

3938
02:56:08,090 --> 02:56:15,090
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: and I was listening to your answer and very happy to hear that ngayon ang ginagawa natin.

3939
02:56:15,090 --> 02:56:22,090
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: Because yung support for SLTs and developmental programs talagang napaka-importante.

3940
02:56:22,090 --> 02:56:25,090
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: Ang ayaw natin is masanay talaga yung mga tao sa dole-outs.

3941
02:56:25,090 --> 02:56:34,090
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: We want the aid coming from the government to really affect and help the families.

3942
02:56:34,090 --> 02:56:45,090
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: While I understand talagang hindi naman pwedeng tanggalin because there are some immediate and emergency needs and assistance na kailangan ibigay at makuha ng mga tao.

3943
02:56:45,090 --> 02:56:51,090
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: But slowly, we also have to integrate. Ngayon nawala na yung ACAP.

3944
02:56:51,090 --> 02:56:57,090
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: Sinama natin sa IX yung 4Ps. I'm talking about yung 4Ps. Sana mas mapalakas natin yung 4Ps.

3945
02:56:57,090 --> 02:57:06,090
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: Dahil yung 4Ps, ang beneficiaryo ng mga 4Ps, kailangan sumunod ka sa RA 11310.

3946
02:57:06,090 --> 02:57:12,090
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: There are strict guidelines, components to this, regulations that has to be followed.

3947
02:57:12,090 --> 02:57:17,090
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: And makikita mo may result because it's not really a dole-out for them.

3948
02:57:17,090 --> 02:57:20,090
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: It encourages and incentivizes families who are benefitting.

3949
02:57:21,090 --> 02:57:29,090
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: So sana ito mapalaki. As correctly pointed out, yung ating sustainable livelihood program, lumeit yung budget.

3950
02:57:29,090 --> 02:57:33,090
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: Pero gusto nga natin palakasin yung mga ganitong programa eh.

3951
02:57:33,090 --> 02:57:45,090
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: So maybe we should put some of the, kung maglalagay ang Congress ng budget, baka dapat dito ilagay instead of additional IX na naman.

3952
02:57:45,090 --> 02:57:49,090
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: Dahil ang gusto natin, slowly.

3953
02:57:49,090 --> 02:57:52,090
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: I think it was pointed out.

3954
02:57:52,090 --> 02:58:06,090
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: Nung nagsimula yung IX program nung panahon ng pandemia, because during the lockout, yung mga extreme lockdowns natin, talaga kahit yung mga gusto magtrabaho, hindi makapagtrabaho.

3955
02:58:06,090 --> 02:58:13,090
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: After a while, nung natapos yung pandemic, hindi nawala yung programa. In fact, mas lumaki pa ito.

3956
02:58:13,090 --> 02:58:17,090
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: But ang ayaw natin sana mangyari is mapag-iwanan yung mga...

3957
02:58:17,090 --> 02:58:18,090
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: ...yung mga...

3958
02:58:19,090 --> 02:58:27,090
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: ...developmental programs which would really lift the family from poverty or help them in a way.

3959
02:58:27,090 --> 02:58:29,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Mr. Chairman, we agree.

3960
02:58:29,090 --> 02:58:32,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The points are well taken.

3961
02:58:32,090 --> 02:58:34,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Just as a quick rundown.

3962
02:58:34,090 --> 02:58:38,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Tama ko kayo that we've been tightening the four-piece, strengthening it.

3963
02:58:38,090 --> 02:58:43,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: In fact, the World Bank last study said nga that it's contributed directly to 2.2 reduction in poverty.

3964
02:58:43,090 --> 02:58:47,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: That's a sign that our implementation has been tightened.

3965
02:58:47,090 --> 02:58:48,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: But I also want to point out na...

3966
02:58:48,090 --> 02:58:51,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Ninabanggit ko ito kanina kay Congressman Tino.

3967
02:58:51,090 --> 02:58:54,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Yesterday's PSA briefing was quite revealing.

3968
02:58:54,090 --> 02:59:05,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Sabi nila na the contributors or the drivers to poverty reduction, one, reduce inflation pre-2026, but also the growth in household income.

3969
02:59:05,090 --> 02:59:08,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: There were five main reasons to it.

3970
02:59:08,090 --> 02:59:14,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: One was yung wages tumaas.

3971
02:59:14,090 --> 02:59:16,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Pangalawa, entrepreneurship.

3972
02:59:16,090 --> 02:59:19,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So nandun na huhulog yung mga SLP natin.

3973
02:59:19,090 --> 02:59:20,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Ibig sabi nakakatulong sila.

3974
02:59:20,090 --> 02:59:21,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And not just us.

3975
02:59:21,090 --> 02:59:27,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: From the small business corporation of DTI, the whole government of approach na DAR, DA, has countryside livelihood.

3976
02:59:27,090 --> 02:59:31,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Lahat yun na pagsasama-sama to entrepreneurship output.

3977
02:59:31,090 --> 02:59:37,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Third lamang, or isa sa pang lima, yung conditional cash transfer na local, which is four-piece.

3978
02:59:37,090 --> 02:59:41,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So meaning, and other transfers, meaning the targeting is working.

3979
02:59:41,090 --> 02:59:44,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Nakakontribute siya pero hindi natin nga gusto yun.

3980
02:59:44,090 --> 02:59:48,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And the other two is foreign remittances and pension.

3981
02:59:48,090 --> 02:59:54,090
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So kung lima yan, sabay ho, nandun yung entrepreneurship and nandun yung cash transfer.

3982
02:59:54,090 --> 03:00:00,160
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And like I agree with you, na dapat we have to wean off the cash transfer gradually while strengthening entrepreneurship.

3983
03:00:01,420 --> 03:00:16,720
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: Okay. And lastly, yung tanong ko lang sa 4Peace. Sir, ilan yung current beneficiary natin ng 4Peace? Ilan yung bagong enrolled sa 4Peace programs? At ilan naman yung mga graduate na sa 4Peace programs?

3984
03:00:16,720 --> 03:00:31,560
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For the record, nung nagsimula ho ang Marcos administration, 4.4 million ho yan. Laging 4.4. So nagtanong ho, since 2014. So since 2014 till 2022, ang napag-graduate lamang po ay 50,000.

3985
03:00:32,440 --> 03:00:46,560
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We're not saying na walang umangatang buhay doon, but they weren't taking the exit mechanism seriously. But under the Marcos Jr. administration, simula ni Sen. Erwin, ngayon naman tinuloy namin, talagang pinag-igtingin natin yung case management.

3986
03:00:46,720 --> 03:01:00,140
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Para yung mga dapat lumabas, lumalabas na. So from 2022 till now, 1.7 million families have already exited. Now, ang natinahong sa database natin, from minus that number, is at around 3 million.

3987
03:01:00,760 --> 03:01:12,820
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Of which, if we are to peg it at the current poverty incidence, dapat 3.5 million na lang sila. Hindi nababalik sa 4.4. So that means by October, we're going to enroll an additional 500,000.

3988
03:01:13,460 --> 03:01:16,700
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: Okay. So, as I mentioned earlier,

3989
03:01:16,720 --> 03:01:39,940
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: Sec. Rec., maraming maraming salamat sa agaran at available na pagtulong doon sa mga calamity-stricken areas doon sa aking lugar. Ito, nasaksihan ko. I'm sure it also happens in other areas, but doon sa distrito ko, meron mga sunog na nangyari nito mga nakaraang buwan at syempre yung pagbabaha.

3990
03:01:39,940 --> 03:01:46,700
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: And I was witness that this, the assistance, kagaya nga ng sleeping care,

3991
03:01:46,720 --> 03:01:58,380
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: yung mga food boxes were readily available at walang nahalong politika. Napunta sa tao yung tulong na kinakailangan nila. Maraming salamat.

3992
03:01:58,880 --> 03:01:59,580
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

3993
03:01:59,580 --> 03:02:00,120
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Thank you, Congressman.

3994
03:02:00,460 --> 03:02:02,880
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Thank you. Thank you, Cong. Buktsutay.

3995
03:02:04,540 --> 03:02:07,720
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Past 12, may we know the pleasure of the Secretary.

3996
03:02:08,420 --> 03:02:11,400
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We can keep on continuing, Mr. Chairman, if that is the wish of the Committee.

3997
03:02:11,580 --> 03:02:13,280
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: We'll do it over working lunch or what?

3998
03:02:13,460 --> 03:02:16,500
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Working lunch is fine, Mr. Chairman. I know there are a lot of members who want to...

3999
03:02:16,720 --> 03:02:18,560
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: So if you need a break, Secretary...

4000
03:02:18,560 --> 03:02:22,820
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: I will call a break. We will respect whatever the decision of the Committee is.

4001
03:02:22,900 --> 03:02:26,520
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: We can have a short break, if you wish.

4002
03:02:27,340 --> 03:02:31,460
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Mr. Chairman, again, if I wish, pwede naman tayo, we can go the distance.

4003
03:02:32,640 --> 03:02:33,480
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Pwede tuloy-tuloy.

4004
03:02:33,660 --> 03:02:35,500
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Okay. So we'll do it.

4005
03:02:37,100 --> 03:02:37,700
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Thank you.

4006
03:02:37,700 --> 03:02:42,060
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: So we'll just have a working lunch for today.

4007
03:02:44,270 --> 03:02:48,010
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Before we proceed, may I recognize our other members?

4008
03:02:48,030 --> 03:02:48,950
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Members who came in.

4009
03:02:49,830 --> 03:02:55,190
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Assistant Minority Leader Iris Montes.

4010
03:02:58,590 --> 03:03:00,870
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Congressman Mark Inverga.

4011
03:03:01,910 --> 03:03:05,430
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: We have Cong. Christine Sison Mian.

4012
03:03:06,550 --> 03:03:09,610
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: We have Deputy Minority Leader Grisel Lagman.

4013
03:03:10,790 --> 03:03:13,530
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: And Representative Mario Jujuy Salvador.

4014
03:03:13,530 --> 03:03:18,290
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: So we proceed.

4015
03:03:19,410 --> 03:03:25,880
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: We now recognize Representative Mila Magsaysay.

4016
03:03:26,240 --> 03:03:26,700
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Ma'am Mila.

4017
03:03:31,030 --> 03:03:32,330
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Mr. Secretary,

4018
03:03:34,330 --> 03:03:37,330
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: just for clarification po,

4019
03:03:38,070 --> 03:03:40,410
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: gusto kong marinig mismo sa inyo,

4020
03:03:40,410 --> 03:03:44,610
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: saan po ba dapat under ang NCSC?

4021
03:03:45,070 --> 03:03:46,950
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Sa Office of the President po ba?

4022
03:03:47,110 --> 03:03:48,390
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: O sa DSWD?

4023
03:03:48,590 --> 03:03:50,410
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Kasi naguguluhan pong mga senior citizens.

4024
03:03:50,410 --> 03:03:57,750
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: At palaging nagtatanong sa akin kung saan talaga under ang senior citizen, ang NCSC.

4025
03:03:58,510 --> 03:04:01,830
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Mr. Chairman, masalimuot ho yung sagot.

4026
03:04:02,130 --> 03:04:04,030
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: I'll try to make it as concise as possible.

4027
03:04:04,190 --> 03:04:07,690
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We will submit to the good committee to be furnished to the good congresswoman

4028
03:04:07,690 --> 03:04:11,130
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: yung legal query ng department sa OP.

4029
03:04:11,730 --> 03:04:15,350
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Kung saan sinabi nila, so to speak, na status quo muna po.

4030
03:04:15,790 --> 03:04:18,710
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Meaning we supervise them, but we should not,

4031
03:04:18,710 --> 03:04:20,210
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: we should not,

4032
03:04:20,410 --> 03:04:24,990
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: we should not directly meddle at this point in time because of the legislation passed.

4033
03:04:25,550 --> 03:04:30,490
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Pero naka-footnote rin doon that the law on optimization has taken into effect

4034
03:04:30,490 --> 03:04:33,490
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and meron na rin hong IRR ng optimization.

4035
03:04:34,310 --> 03:04:38,110
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So meaning nothing stops the department from submitting an optimization plan

4036
03:04:38,110 --> 03:04:40,450
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: up until na-approve yung optimization plan

4037
03:04:40,450 --> 03:04:44,330
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: tsaka lang namin makukuha yung full control and authority over NCSC.

4038
03:04:44,490 --> 03:04:47,590
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So for now, it's status quo na independent ho sila sa amin.

4039
03:04:47,590 --> 03:04:50,210
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: They are merely coordinating with us.

4040
03:04:50,410 --> 03:04:52,330
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For programs and for budget purposes.

4041
03:04:53,410 --> 03:04:55,250
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For budget purposes also.

4042
03:04:55,990 --> 03:04:59,670
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For budget purposes, nakasama ho sila sa araw pero ng talakay,

4043
03:04:59,850 --> 03:05:01,670
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: pero nakahiwalay ho naman silang line item.

4044
03:05:02,490 --> 03:05:10,250
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Kasi sa batas po kasi, under ng Office of the President, ang NCSC.

4045
03:05:11,030 --> 03:05:14,790
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: So coordination lang po sa DSWD.

4046
03:05:16,290 --> 03:05:17,590
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Coordination lamang po.

4047
03:05:18,250 --> 03:05:20,390
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: That's been very clear by the legal opinion.

4048
03:05:20,410 --> 03:05:23,370
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The opinion of the Office of the President when we did the query like yourself.

4049
03:05:24,450 --> 03:05:29,050
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Yes po. Kasi sa sulat po kasi ni Executive Secretary Ralph Recto,

4050
03:05:29,570 --> 03:05:34,370
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: lateral relationship, parang coordination lang po ng programs and parties.

4051
03:05:34,370 --> 03:05:39,030
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Correct. But if you look at that same letter, meron ho yung caveat on optimization.

4052
03:05:39,790 --> 03:05:42,170
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So lumabas na ho recently yung IRR ng optimization.

4053
03:05:42,570 --> 03:05:45,930
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So we did submit our optimization plan that will include NCSC.

4054
03:05:45,930 --> 03:05:49,610
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Okay. Thank you. Thank you, Mr. Secretary.

4055
03:05:50,410 --> 03:05:55,230
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: And at least na-klaro po kung ano po ang ano ng NCSC.

4056
03:05:55,850 --> 03:06:02,550
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: And number two po, marami po akong reklamong natanggap na sobrang bagal at tagal po

4057
03:06:02,550 --> 03:06:08,250
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: ng accreditation process ng mga home care at elderly facilities.

4058
03:06:08,710 --> 03:06:10,770
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Ano po kaya ang nagiging problema?

4059
03:06:11,570 --> 03:06:14,870
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: I can tell you point blank that we've streamlined it already.

4060
03:06:15,270 --> 03:06:20,070
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Kami na ho siguro may pinaka maikling timetable kapag ka kompleto at pumapasok.

4061
03:06:20,410 --> 03:06:24,510
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Pumapasa. Minsan ho kasi nagre-reklamo pero I can show you if you can give us the names

4062
03:06:24,510 --> 03:06:27,270
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: na minsan hindi ho pumapasa and we have to be very careful.

4063
03:06:28,150 --> 03:06:32,010
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Hindi ho pwedeng i-insist na gusto nila, gusto nila because kami naman ho ang madadali.

4064
03:06:32,150 --> 03:06:37,390
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Kung may pinalusot kaming accreditation na hindi pumapasa sa standards prescribed by the department.

4065
03:06:38,150 --> 03:06:41,870
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Alam niyo ho, Mr. Chairman, it used to take almost six months to one year

4066
03:06:41,870 --> 03:06:45,930
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: to get a SWADA accredited, registered license and accredited.

4067
03:06:46,170 --> 03:06:48,650
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Kami, as fast as two months time.

4068
03:06:49,290 --> 03:06:49,810
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Tapos?

4069
03:06:49,930 --> 03:06:50,170
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Yes.

4070
03:06:50,170 --> 03:06:52,210
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: As long as you pass the standards.

4071
03:06:52,430 --> 03:06:57,510
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Kaya lang minsan ho kasi they will insist na pasado sila but our recommendation is hindi sila pasado.

4072
03:06:57,910 --> 03:07:01,110
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So doon ho talaga tumatagal but we do provide technical assistance.

4073
03:07:01,550 --> 03:07:06,630
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: If susundan naman nila yung mga recommendation namin, mapapabilis at makukuha nila yung kanilang accreditation.

4074
03:07:07,350 --> 03:07:08,930
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Thank you, Mr. Secretary.

4075
03:07:09,350 --> 03:07:12,070
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And digital rin ho ang aming application.

4076
03:07:12,390 --> 03:07:16,050
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Streamlined, meaning when you register, sabay na ho ang license to operate.

4077
03:07:16,050 --> 03:07:18,430
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So two weeks, ay two months lang.

4078
03:07:18,650 --> 03:07:20,110
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Kung pumapasa po.

4079
03:07:20,170 --> 03:07:21,410
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And it's all done online.

4080
03:07:21,570 --> 03:07:24,270
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Hindi na humano-mano na dinadaanan sa office yung mga requirements.

4081
03:07:25,310 --> 03:07:26,230
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Thank you.

4082
03:07:26,810 --> 03:07:37,530
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Number three, Secretary, under our existing laws po, mayroon pong 1% budget allocation for senior citizens at PWDs

4083
03:07:37,530 --> 03:07:41,110
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: ang bawat ahensya ng National Government Agency.

4084
03:07:41,650 --> 03:07:47,170
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Mayroon po bang monitoring mechanism ang DSWD kung paano po ito nagagamit?

4085
03:07:48,050 --> 03:07:49,630
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Madam Chair,

4086
03:07:50,170 --> 03:07:54,230
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We signed a joint memo circular with DBM on its implementation.

4087
03:07:54,390 --> 03:07:59,070
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And I believe it's DBM through the submissions ng mga ahensya na nagmumonitor ng 1% compliance.

4088
03:08:00,590 --> 03:08:05,670
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: So, nagpapakinabangan naman po ng mga senior citizens.

4089
03:08:06,190 --> 03:08:07,430
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And slash PWD.

4090
03:08:08,550 --> 03:08:09,070
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Thank you.

4091
03:08:10,250 --> 03:08:15,610
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: And number four po, napakarami pong mga reklamo hanggang ngayon

4092
03:08:15,610 --> 03:08:19,610
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: ang mga mahal nating senior citizens tungkol sa payout ng social payout.

4093
03:08:20,170 --> 03:08:22,310
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Pension para sa mga indigent.

4094
03:08:22,750 --> 03:08:24,770
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Ano na po ba ang nangyari?

4095
03:08:25,290 --> 03:08:28,710
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Mr. Chair, yan yung kaninang pinaliliwanag ko kay Congressman Ordanez

4096
03:08:28,710 --> 03:08:33,070
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: na unfortunately, the most of the grievances is inclusion.

4097
03:08:34,070 --> 03:08:39,710
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, minsan nahihirapan ho kami dahil nga una, kalahati lang naman ho ang funded nung mandate.

4098
03:08:39,870 --> 03:08:40,530
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Hindi naman ho buo.

4099
03:08:41,170 --> 03:08:47,170
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Ibig sabihin, sa dami ho na kailangan i-accommodate, kalahati lang ho lagi taon-taon ang naibibigay sa amin.

4100
03:08:48,010 --> 03:08:49,730
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Pangalawa, siyempre ho minsan lack of information,

4101
03:08:50,170 --> 03:08:57,310
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: nasa-strike off sila sa listahan dahil nga meron silang SSS, GSIS, or other types of pension

4102
03:08:57,310 --> 03:09:02,430
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: na hindi nila naunawaan na pag may ganun ka na kasi maliit lang naman, feeling nila entitled sila

4103
03:09:02,430 --> 03:09:05,350
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and we personally agree, naaalis sila sa listahan.

4104
03:09:05,490 --> 03:09:09,050
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And third, yung problema nga ho sa CBMS tulad na nabanggit namin kanina,

4105
03:09:09,170 --> 03:09:13,110
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: which we've remedied already because nga ngayon, meron ng on-demand purpose

4106
03:09:13,110 --> 03:09:18,110
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: meaning pag binigay sa amin ng LGN listahan, magka-query na lang kami, maaring wala ka sa CBMS

4107
03:09:18,110 --> 03:09:25,110
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: pero pag nasa birth registry ka at wala ka naman sa death registry at ikaw ay matanda na, kasama ka ho kagad.

4108
03:09:26,150 --> 03:09:31,450
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Okay po, kasi yun nga po, yung mga nagbawas kayo, kasi dapat lang humagbawas kayo

4109
03:09:31,450 --> 03:09:36,270
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: kasi may mga nagpe-pension, may mga medyo mayaman na tumatanggap, no?

4110
03:09:36,650 --> 03:09:41,270
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Pero ano pong nangyari, ano pong ba ang gagawin natin dun sa mga nabawas?

4111
03:09:41,430 --> 03:09:45,230
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Hindi ho ba pwedeng doon din iibalik yung mga nabawas?

4112
03:09:46,230 --> 03:09:46,830
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Again,

4113
03:09:48,110 --> 03:09:54,130
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Again, we have to be, we have to look at the age kasi yung bagong guidelines namin, age muna.

4114
03:09:54,730 --> 03:09:57,810
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: I think you would agree na unahin natin yung pinakamatatanda.

4115
03:09:57,990 --> 03:10:02,850
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So yung mga na-free up na slot, hinahanap namin sa CBMS yung 90 pababa

4116
03:10:02,850 --> 03:10:07,570
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and then inuunti-unti namin malagay sila sa listahan.

4117
03:10:09,700 --> 03:10:12,720
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So it's not geographic in short, it's age.

4118
03:10:13,280 --> 03:10:17,740
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So titignan namin yung CBMS at yung mga waitlist, unahin natin yung mga pinakamatatanda

4119
03:10:17,740 --> 03:10:19,220
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and I think that's the most equitable.

4120
03:10:19,420 --> 03:10:22,540
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: At this point in time, nakalahati lang yung funded nung mandate.

4121
03:10:22,920 --> 03:10:26,280
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Siguro mas maganda na ho, siguro universal social pension.

4122
03:10:26,280 --> 03:10:29,000
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And we totally agree 101%.

4123
03:10:29,000 --> 03:10:32,600
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Ang mga seniors, lahat na po sila tatanggap na po.

4124
03:10:33,280 --> 03:10:39,220
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: So, paano po ba karami ang ma-existing at operational senior citizens

4125
03:10:39,220 --> 03:10:41,900
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: o elderly facilities natin nationwide?

4126
03:10:42,600 --> 03:10:49,360
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Paano po ang budget allocation determination ng mga DSW-run elderly facilities sa buong bansa?

4127
03:10:49,420 --> 03:10:57,120
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Matagal po na pong binabanggit, kailangan natin ng mas maraming mga residential homes

4128
03:10:57,120 --> 03:11:02,360
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: and facilities for senior citizens who are abandoned, homeless, and neglected.

4129
03:11:03,060 --> 03:11:06,040
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Ano po ang naging hakbang na ninyo dito?

4130
03:11:18,280 --> 03:11:21,480
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We have four nationwide and admittedly kulang po ito.

4131
03:11:21,740 --> 03:11:23,400
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And that's why we're asking for more budget.

4132
03:11:23,560 --> 03:11:27,120
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Pero tulad din ang paliwanag ko kanina, we are now taking, based on last year's budget,

4133
03:11:27,660 --> 03:11:29,620
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: we are now taking a PPP approach to it.

4134
03:11:29,620 --> 03:11:30,000
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Meaning?

4135
03:11:30,820 --> 03:11:32,300
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Meron na kaming cost of care provision.

4136
03:11:32,300 --> 03:11:35,720
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Kung saan, kung meron namang private na pwede natin doon i-refer,

4137
03:11:36,060 --> 03:11:37,960
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: DSWD ho magbabayad ng cost of care.

4138
03:11:38,300 --> 03:11:41,420
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Kasi mas mabilis, mas effective yung pagtatayo ng gano'n.

4139
03:11:41,480 --> 03:11:43,200
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We're almost done with the guidelines.

4140
03:11:43,360 --> 03:11:46,600
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We're just waiting for the final go signal from the DBM.

4141
03:11:47,660 --> 03:11:47,820
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Yeah.

4142
03:11:48,280 --> 03:11:53,280
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Four for the nationally-run residential care facility.

4143
03:11:53,860 --> 03:11:56,820
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Three for the LG-run residential care facility.

4144
03:11:57,260 --> 03:11:58,580
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Seven na po lahat.

4145
03:11:58,580 --> 03:12:00,800
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: So, sana po matagdagan natin.

4146
03:12:00,820 --> 03:12:04,700
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Kasi ang dami po tayong abandoned and homeless senior citizens.

4147
03:12:04,700 --> 03:12:05,180
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: And we agree.

4148
03:12:06,240 --> 03:12:07,320
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Thank you po.

4149
03:12:07,800 --> 03:12:15,060
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: At nito pong mga nakaraang mga linggo, sunod-sunod po ang mga pagulan at pagbaha

4150
03:12:15,060 --> 03:12:16,700
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: dahil sa habagat.

4151
03:12:17,040 --> 03:12:22,140
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Nasusunod po ba sa distribution ng mga relief goods or family food packs

4152
03:12:22,140 --> 03:12:24,680
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: na priority ang mga senior citizens?

4153
03:12:25,200 --> 03:12:27,700
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Tila hindi po ito nangyayari, Secretary.

4154
03:12:27,700 --> 03:12:30,600
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Parang hindi po talagang mahal ng DSWD ang mga senior citizens.

4155
03:12:30,820 --> 03:12:36,040
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Mahal na mahal namin ang mga senior citizens, lalo na po kayo.

4156
03:12:36,780 --> 03:12:39,940
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Mr. Chairman, we have to remember.

4157
03:12:40,940 --> 03:12:46,140
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Sa batas sa Local Government Code, ang first responder po talaga ang mga local government units.

4158
03:12:46,840 --> 03:12:52,100
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Ang ginagawa lamang ng DSWD is to augment kasi kulang ang kapasidad ng mga LGU.

4159
03:12:52,100 --> 03:13:00,400
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We're proud to say that this tong mga habagat, 3.6 million na family food packs ang lumabas in a span of four months.

4160
03:13:00,820 --> 03:13:05,420
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Ibinabagsak po natin yun sa mga local government units for them to do the last mile distribution.

4161
03:13:05,960 --> 03:13:09,420
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Dahil wala naman ho kaming sapat na tao to do that or know-how ng terrain.

4162
03:13:09,940 --> 03:13:16,660
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Now, we constantly remind our local social welfare offices to prioritize vulnerable sectors.

4163
03:13:17,200 --> 03:13:22,380
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Seniors, people with disability, indigenous people, pregnant and lactating women.

4164
03:13:22,380 --> 03:13:28,340
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Pati sa camp management kung saan nagaganap ang pinakamarami na aktividad during an evacuation,

4165
03:13:29,120 --> 03:13:30,780
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: kine-remind din ho namin sila sa protocols.

4166
03:13:30,820 --> 03:13:35,440
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Kasi, we set the standards, they execute it, we regulate them.

4167
03:13:36,580 --> 03:13:39,500
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Pero sa 3.6 million na sana all na ho yun.

4168
03:13:39,600 --> 03:13:44,320
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, we would assume na dapat nabigyan ho ng mga local government units yung kanila mga senior.

4169
03:13:44,480 --> 03:13:48,220
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And alam ko mahal na mahal ng mga local government units ang kanila mga senior citizens.

4170
03:13:48,240 --> 03:13:52,520
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Yes, because seniors are the most vulnerable sectors when it comes to calamity.

4171
03:13:52,520 --> 03:14:00,520
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: So, for the record, Mr. Chair, I just want to put this in the record that I would like to...

4172
03:14:00,820 --> 03:14:09,820
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: to file a complaint against Region 1 Director Angela Gopela for her arrogance and her...

4173
03:14:11,100 --> 03:14:14,120
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: and doing injustice to the senior citizens.

4174
03:14:14,740 --> 03:14:15,820
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

4175
03:14:16,140 --> 03:14:19,640
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Mr. Chairman, we will accept and we will commission the necessary fact-finding

4176
03:14:19,640 --> 03:14:24,040
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and go through our administrative process and we will report back to the committee.

4177
03:14:24,580 --> 03:14:26,840
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Thank you. She doesn't deserve that position.

4178
03:14:28,380 --> 03:14:30,320
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Thank you. Thank you, Kuwang Mila.

4179
03:14:30,820 --> 03:14:35,140
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Thank you, Mr. Chair. That's all.

4180
03:14:36,200 --> 03:14:39,980
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Maybe, can we take up already the budget of the NCOC or later?

4181
03:14:41,060 --> 03:14:44,780
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Maybe later. I think it's already incorporated.

4182
03:14:45,360 --> 03:14:46,460
Rep. Milagros "Mila" Aquino-Magsaysay: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

4183
03:15:07,860 --> 03:15:27,200
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: We now recognize Cong. Elijah San Fernando. Is he around? No. So, Representative Edgar Erice...

4184
03:15:27,200 --> 03:15:35,990
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Is he around? Representative Iris Montes.

4185
03:15:35,990 --> 03:15:38,380
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you, Mr. Chair. Um...

4186
03:15:38,380 --> 03:15:46,120
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Magandang tanghali po, Secretary Rex, and to the whole DSWD family. Most of my questions

4187
03:15:46,120 --> 03:15:52,060
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: have been previously asked and have been adequately answered by the secretary so i just have

4188
03:15:52,060 --> 03:16:00,620
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: one simple question but before um i i asked that um i was just requested by our colleague

4189
03:16:00,620 --> 03:16:05,920
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Congresswoman Johanne Monich Bautista to ask about her concern

4190
03:16:05,920 --> 03:16:09,260
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Tungkol po ito, Secretary, sa QRF.

4191
03:16:09,260 --> 03:16:12,800
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Sa presentation po kasi mapapansin natin,

4192
03:16:12,800 --> 03:16:14,400
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: like for 2025,

4193
03:16:14,400 --> 03:16:16,100
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: yung regular niyo po

4194
03:16:16,100 --> 03:16:42,710
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: is 1.25 billion. Tapos nagkaroon po ng replenishment ng 7.8. Sa 2026, 3 billion po, nagkaroon ng replenishment na 9.6. Ang concern lang po ng ating colleague ay for 2027, 1.25 lang daw po. Hindi po ba daw kukulangin? Assured po daw tayo ba na kahit maliit ito ay magre-replenish ulit?

4195
03:16:42,710 --> 03:17:10,740
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Mr. Chairman, it's a very good question. Nagagalak ho kami sa tanong na 'yan. Actually, may assurance naman ho na may pondo kasi replenishable. Pero siyempre sa panahon ng sakuna dapat mabilis ho kami, maagap. So nakikiusap ho kami, sumulat rin kami sa committee na sana ma-restore back to its 3 billion level. At dati napagbigyan naman ho kami para mas mabilis kami na nakaka-responde, lalo na sabay-sabay ho yung sakuna. It's no longer contained in one area; it's multi-region.

4196
03:17:10,740 --> 03:17:11,940
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So sana ho mabalik ho talaga kami.

4197
03:17:11,940 --> 03:17:16,100
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We are earnestly asking the committee to consider because ho

4198
03:17:16,100 --> 03:17:23,680
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: maaapektuhan yung turnaround time namin sa pag-responde, pag-procure, paglatag ng emergency cash transfer.

4199
03:17:24,180 --> 03:17:32,080
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And I want to point out, para lang sa kaalaman ng lahat, wala namang dagdag na cost sa gobyerno dahil nandun lang siya nakalagak sa QRF ng national.

4200
03:17:32,580 --> 03:17:37,560
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, sana lang lakihan yung seed capital ng QRF namin para mas mabilis kaming makaresponde.

4201
03:17:37,560 --> 03:17:48,320
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you, Secretary. This representation shares your sentiments and I do support that we restore your 2026 QRF levels.

4202
03:17:49,420 --> 03:17:55,960
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Moving on to my question, a simple question, Mr. Chair.

4203
03:17:57,580 --> 03:18:06,960
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: The DSWD has repeatedly faced challenges in ensuring timely and targeted delivery of social protection programs.

4204
03:18:07,560 --> 03:18:17,380
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yan po ay nasabi nyo na, nabanggit nyo na during the lead committee hearings at kanina po, parang nire-iterate po ninyo uli.

4205
03:18:17,900 --> 03:18:23,420
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Dahil po, meron tayong fragmented and disconnected data system.

4206
03:18:24,180 --> 03:18:30,400
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, wala po tayong real-time na accurate na data.

4207
03:18:30,400 --> 03:18:36,800
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, medyo nahihirapan po tayo to roll out sa part po ninyo yung mga social protection programs.

4208
03:18:37,000 --> 03:18:37,320
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ano po?

4209
03:18:37,560 --> 03:18:50,100
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: That is why this representation, ang kababaihan kabalikatan para sa kapakanan at kaunlaran ng bayan, actively participated during the lead committee hearings.

4210
03:18:50,680 --> 03:19:00,600
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Out of that, the 4K has filed at least six or seven interventions, one of which is House Bill 9084.

4211
03:19:00,600 --> 03:19:06,600
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: It calls for the establishment of a national and integrated registry system.

4212
03:19:07,560 --> 03:19:10,700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: That is interoperable to address this gap.

4213
03:19:11,340 --> 03:19:17,640
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, the system establishes the foundational mechanism for efficient, transparent, and responsive governance.

4214
03:19:17,640 --> 03:19:36,720
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: It also proposes a system that builds on existing national initiatives, such as the Philippine identification system and social registries, transforming them into a unified data ecosystem that supports inclusive growth and digital transformation.

4215
03:19:37,560 --> 03:19:47,700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, it also addresses the long-standing fragmentation of government data systems, which limit efficiency and effectiveness of public service delivery.

4216
03:19:48,140 --> 03:20:05,700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: But beyond Mr. Secretary, a single registry, what the country truly needs is an integrated yet interoperable system that connects administrative registries like LGU household records, barangay level data,

4217
03:20:05,700 --> 03:20:12,560
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: data, sa civil registration and identification systems naman po, nakapaloob sana doon yung

4218
03:20:12,560 --> 03:20:16,560
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: PhilSys, birth and death records, and national ID.

4219
03:20:17,380 --> 03:20:22,600
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Dapat meron din po sigurong component na sectoral and program-based registries.

4220
03:20:23,260 --> 03:20:30,220
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Nandoon po yung 4Ps, yung senior citizen, yung PWDs, meron pong disaster response list,

4221
03:20:30,620 --> 03:20:32,960
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: education, and labor database.

4222
03:20:32,960 --> 03:20:37,900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Sa social registry naman po, dapat meron mga poverty targeting mechanism,

4223
03:20:38,480 --> 03:20:47,820
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: household vulnerability mapping, meron din pong PhilHealth, GSIS, SSS, DepEd, DOLE, and LGU databases.

4224
03:20:48,160 --> 03:20:56,660
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, only by linking the systems can we ensure real-time, accurate, and inclusive targeting of beneficiaries,

4225
03:20:56,660 --> 03:21:02,120
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: while also, kapaloob din po doon sa bill, pag-safeguard ng data privacy and accountability.

4226
03:21:02,120 --> 03:21:13,220
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, ang simpleng tanong ko lamang po, Mr. Secretary, does the department view this integration as a step towards the right direction?

4227
03:21:13,780 --> 03:21:17,120
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: And will the Secretary support this reform?

4228
03:21:17,800 --> 03:21:25,920
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Mr. Chairman, in fact, we are doing a small pilot inside the department, a social registry that integrates our own databases

4229
03:21:25,920 --> 03:21:28,760
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: from 4Ps, Walang Gutong, the program databases.

4230
03:21:28,760 --> 03:21:31,560
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: But it would be nice if it's scaled up to a national level.

4231
03:21:31,560 --> 03:21:32,880
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And we're fully supportive.

4232
03:21:33,760 --> 03:21:36,760
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Maraming salamat po, Mr. Secretary, Mr. Chair.

4233
03:21:37,460 --> 03:21:40,160
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: I will furnish you po a copy of my bill.

4234
03:21:40,460 --> 03:21:45,160
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: And I will appreciate if you can take a good look at it.

4235
03:21:45,460 --> 03:21:52,760
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: And siguro po, you can share, you can review, send some comments and inputs to improve the bill.

4236
03:21:53,060 --> 03:22:01,160
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: And if you find it helpful and necessary, perhaps I will just request the Secretary to bring it up, perhaps, to the Executive.

4237
03:22:01,160 --> 03:22:10,060
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Department for its passage or for it to be a priority of this Congress.

4238
03:22:10,060 --> 03:22:12,560
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you, Secretary Rex.

4239
03:22:12,560 --> 03:22:18,360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Mr. Chair, we'll gladly accept that we already registered our full support to the bill in writing early on.

4240
03:22:18,360 --> 03:22:22,060
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, we'll gladly accept and see if there are new angles that you want us to comment on.

4241
03:22:23,940 --> 03:22:26,040
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you, Mr. Chair, that would be all.

4242
03:22:27,840 --> 03:22:28,540
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Thank you.

4243
03:22:39,710 --> 03:22:41,310
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: May we recognize

4244
03:22:42,910 --> 03:22:44,710
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Representative

4245
03:22:45,010 --> 03:22:46,910
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Johanne Monich Bautista.

4246
03:22:48,110 --> 03:22:49,410
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

4247
03:22:49,410 --> 03:22:54,810
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: And magandang hapon po sa DSWD family, Secretary Rex Gatchalian.

4248
03:22:56,410 --> 03:23:00,010
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: I believe my, one of my questions was asked earlier by Kong Iris.

4249
03:23:00,010 --> 03:23:01,110
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: Thank you very much po.

4250
03:23:01,110 --> 03:23:04,710
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: I akala ko po hindi ako makakabalik agad, but now I'm here.

4251
03:23:05,110 --> 03:23:10,610
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: I just wanted to join my colleagues who already expressed their

4252
03:23:12,010 --> 03:23:12,710
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: support.

4253
03:23:12,910 --> 03:23:19,310
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: And commendation to the DSWD family, of course, under the outstanding leadership of Secretary

4254
03:23:19,310 --> 03:23:24,010
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: Rex Gatchalian for their timely and effective delivery of social services.

4255
03:23:24,010 --> 03:23:30,010
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: Kitang-kita po natin sa bawat sakuna, sa bawat trahedya po, nandyan po on the ground, always

4256
03:23:30,010 --> 03:23:32,410
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: at the forefront ang ating DSWD.

4257
03:23:32,410 --> 03:23:34,710
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: Maraming salamat po sa inyong servisyo.

4258
03:23:34,710 --> 03:23:42,410
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: And with that, I express my full support para po sa budget ng DSWD.

4259
03:23:42,410 --> 03:23:45,310
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: Marami pa pong mga kailangang idagdag.

4260
03:23:45,310 --> 03:23:49,710
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: Nabanggit na po kanina, kagaya po nung AICS, hindi ko na po babanggitin kasi I believe

4261
03:23:49,710 --> 03:23:59,510
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: as Secrex was able to explain and justify the need to at least return the amount that

4262
03:23:59,510 --> 03:24:01,310
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: was removed under the NEP.

4263
03:24:01,310 --> 03:24:09,010
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: And then yung QRF din po na nabanggit ni Kong Iris Montes kanina, nakita naman po natin,

4264
03:24:09,010 --> 03:24:11,510
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: quick response, importante po yan.

4265
03:24:11,510 --> 03:24:17,410
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: Kita naman din po natin na itong pondong po ito ay diretsyo naman po yan sa mga tao.

4266
03:24:17,410 --> 03:24:25,410
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: So tayo po ay hindi po dapat magdalawang isip at maging panatag po tayo kung dadagdagan

4267
03:24:25,410 --> 03:24:29,410
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: po natin ang pondong ito na kailangan po ng DSWD.

4268
03:24:29,410 --> 03:24:36,410
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: Siguro po just one more question, since natanong na po yung QRF kanina.

4269
03:24:36,410 --> 03:24:40,410
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: On behalf lang po ng ating mga workers po.

4270
03:24:40,410 --> 03:24:48,310
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: Mr. Chair, kasi po siguro the good secretary can explain.

4271
03:24:48,310 --> 03:24:56,310
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: Ang hinanaing po kasi ng iba po sa ating mga workers, sinasabi po nila na they feel like

4272
03:24:56,310 --> 03:25:02,310
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: minsan po na pag iiwanan sila pagdating sa mga social services po ng ating gobyerno.

4273
03:25:02,310 --> 03:25:08,310
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: Dahil of course hindi ko naman po sinasabi na definitely priority po natin yung mga higit

4274
03:25:08,310 --> 03:25:09,310
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: na nangangailangan.

4275
03:25:09,310 --> 03:25:17,210
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: But then we also have our minimum wage earners, even our middle class workers na isang emergency,

4276
03:25:17,210 --> 03:25:25,210
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: medical emergency lang, isang namatayan ay maapektuhan na po ang kanilang finances.

4277
03:25:25,210 --> 03:25:34,210
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: So maybe the good secretary can explain or inform our minimum wage workers, yung pong

4278
03:25:34,210 --> 03:25:37,210
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: mga nagtatrabaho nating mga kababayan.

4279
03:25:37,210 --> 03:25:39,210
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: That they are also covered.

4280
03:25:39,310 --> 03:25:42,210
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: And entitled to the programs of the DSWD.

4281
03:25:42,210 --> 03:25:46,210
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Mr. Chairman, I just want to again point out na ang AICS ho is for everybody.

4282
03:25:46,210 --> 03:25:50,210
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: It looks at the crisis situation more than the income level.

4283
03:25:50,210 --> 03:25:55,210
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So lagi namin sinasabi magtungo lang ho sa aming mga tanggapan para ma-assess ng social

4284
03:25:55,210 --> 03:25:56,210
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: worker natin.

4285
03:25:56,210 --> 03:25:58,210
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And in fact, I just don't have the data with me.

4286
03:25:58,210 --> 03:26:00,210
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We will gladly furnish the committee.

4287
03:26:00,210 --> 03:26:05,210
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: A percentage, a real significant percentage of AIICS really goes to those above the middle

4288
03:26:05,210 --> 03:26:06,210
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: class.

4289
03:26:06,210 --> 03:26:08,310
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So those above the poverty threshold, the near poor.

4290
03:26:08,310 --> 03:26:09,210
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: All the way to 50%.

4291
03:26:09,310 --> 03:26:13,210
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: I just don't have the percentages right now but we'll send it to you.

4292
03:26:13,210 --> 03:26:19,210
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: It goes to show na yung crisis in crisis situation yung tinitignan.

4293
03:26:19,210 --> 03:26:25,210
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Now number two, the president also instructed us to widen the lalo na ngayong energy emergency.

4294
03:26:25,210 --> 03:26:31,210
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: That's why the uplift assistance has three components to it of which yung pangatlo is

4295
03:26:31,210 --> 03:26:33,210
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: targeting low wage earners.

4296
03:26:33,210 --> 03:26:36,210
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: These are above minimum wage earners ng SSS.

4297
03:26:36,210 --> 03:26:38,210
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: That's around 1.5 million.

4298
03:26:38,210 --> 03:26:46,110
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Ang na-service na namin around 800,000 kasi tulad na nabanggit ko kanina dormant yung beneficiary

4299
03:26:46,110 --> 03:26:48,110
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: accounts ng marami sa kanila.

4300
03:26:48,110 --> 03:26:53,110
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: But we're working on that with SSS to try to look for more of them para ma-exhaust natin

4301
03:26:53,110 --> 03:27:00,210
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: yung 1.5 the monthly allocation na tigta 2,000 para sa ating mga SSS low wage earners.

4302
03:27:00,210 --> 03:27:01,210
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: Thank you po.

4303
03:27:01,210 --> 03:27:06,210
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: And thank you for that explanation po from our Secretary Rex Gatchalian.

4304
03:27:06,210 --> 03:27:07,210
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: I think yun lang po.

4305
03:27:07,210 --> 03:27:09,110
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: I think yun lang po ang aking ipo-point out.

4306
03:27:09,110 --> 03:27:11,110
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: Nasagot naman po.

4307
03:27:11,110 --> 03:27:18,110
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: And again, I just wanted to manifest our sincere appreciation to the good Secretary and the

4308
03:27:18,110 --> 03:27:22,110
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: entire DSWD family for all their hard work 24-7.

4309
03:27:22,110 --> 03:27:25,110
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: Mapaulan, mapabagyo, nandyan po sila.

4310
03:27:25,110 --> 03:27:31,110
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: Maraming salamat po and we manifest our strong support for the needed budget and the requested

4311
03:27:31,110 --> 03:27:33,110
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: additional budget of the DSWD.

4312
03:27:33,110 --> 03:27:35,110
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: Maraming salamat po, Mr. Chair.

4313
03:27:35,740 --> 03:27:36,670
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

4314
03:27:37,210 --> 03:27:39,110
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Thank you.

4315
03:27:41,940 --> 03:27:46,730
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: We now recognize Representative Krisel Lagman.

4316
03:27:49,160 --> 03:27:50,980
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

4317
03:27:50,980 --> 03:27:52,840
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Hindi pa kumakain si Secretary.

4318
03:27:52,840 --> 03:28:01,840
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Iba talaga pag rooted sa local government ang head ng department.

4319
03:28:01,840 --> 03:28:04,840
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Lalong-lalo na pagdating sa social services.

4320
03:28:04,840 --> 03:28:10,840
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Damang-dama po namin ang hands-on approach

4321
03:28:10,840 --> 03:28:14,740
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: and holistic approach ng inyong paggogobyerno, Secretary Rex.

4322
03:28:14,740 --> 03:28:22,740
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Ang Tabaco, Albay, laging nasasalanta.

4323
03:28:22,740 --> 03:28:25,740
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Maging bagyo man yan o mga volcanic eruptions.

4324
03:28:25,740 --> 03:28:35,740
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Itong nakaraan ang pinakamahaba na evacuation time sa loob ng evacuation centers.

4325
03:28:35,740 --> 03:28:38,740
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Inabot po sa 7 buwan.

4326
03:28:38,740 --> 03:28:39,740
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: 7 buwan.

4327
03:28:39,740 --> 03:28:45,640
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Nagsimula ng January 6 at nag-decamp ng August 6.

4328
03:28:45,640 --> 03:28:47,640
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: So, 7 months po.

4329
03:28:47,640 --> 03:28:51,640
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: And hindi po talaga nagpabaya ang DSWD.

4330
03:28:51,640 --> 03:28:55,640
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Naandito ang aming regional director, si RD Norman Laurio.

4331
03:28:55,640 --> 03:29:05,640
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: And nagpapasalamat po ako sa agaran at maliksi na pag-responde niya sa mga pangailangan ng aming mga evacuees.

4332
03:29:05,640 --> 03:29:09,640
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Suficiente rin po yung pinamimigay.

4333
03:29:09,740 --> 03:29:20,640
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: In fact, every 15 days, may binibigay na good for 3 days na food packs.

4334
03:29:20,640 --> 03:29:29,640
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: So, sa isang buwan, nakaka-receive ng mga around 9 to 10 boxes ang aming mga families.

4335
03:29:29,640 --> 03:29:32,640
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Ito lang po ang aking comment.

4336
03:29:32,640 --> 03:29:35,640
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: First is, wala pong pinipili.

4337
03:29:35,640 --> 03:29:39,540
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Ang ibig kong sabihin, maging isang miyembro lang ng pamilya,

4338
03:29:39,540 --> 03:29:41,440
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: o sampung miyembro ng pamilya,

4339
03:29:41,440 --> 03:29:45,440
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: eh ang ibinabahagi po ay isang kahon.

4340
03:29:45,440 --> 03:29:49,440
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: And every 3 days po sila nakaka-receive nito.

4341
03:29:49,440 --> 03:29:55,440
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Baka maaari po na maging mas maayos ang pagbabahagi nito.

4342
03:29:55,440 --> 03:29:59,440
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Kasi ang isang pamilya na may isang miyembro,

4343
03:30:00,000 --> 03:30:10,440
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: At makakareceive ng 6 kilos of rice every 3 days ay napakalaki po na appropriation na sana ay napunta doon sa mas malalaking pamilya.

4344
03:30:10,920 --> 03:30:12,640
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: So, iyon po ang isang comment ko.

4345
03:30:13,180 --> 03:30:15,320
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Pangalawa rin naman po yung variety.

4346
03:30:15,680 --> 03:30:18,900
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Alam ko kakaiba ang sitwasyon namin sa Albay.

4347
03:30:18,900 --> 03:30:24,040
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Hindi all the time ay ganito kahaba ang evacuation.

4348
03:30:25,500 --> 03:30:28,920
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Ang iba ilang araw lang, baka linggo.

4349
03:30:28,920 --> 03:30:32,200
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Pero nangyayari po at nangyayari pa lang.

4350
03:30:32,420 --> 03:30:38,180
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Kaya ang pakiusap ko po sana may variety rin ang laman ng mga boxes natin.

4351
03:30:40,420 --> 03:30:45,380
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: And sana po naandito ang chairman ng Ways and Means Committee.

4352
03:30:45,380 --> 03:30:48,140
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Katabi ko po si chairman.

4353
03:30:48,940 --> 03:30:56,640
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: And napansin po namin ay yung madali pong ma-distribute at matagal ang shelf life ang nilalagay natin.

4354
03:30:56,820 --> 03:30:57,160
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Siyempre.

4355
03:30:57,500 --> 03:30:58,840
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Kasi mahabaan.

4356
03:30:58,920 --> 03:31:00,300
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Ang storage nito.

4357
03:31:00,740 --> 03:31:10,000
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Subalit sana po instead of 3-in-1 coffee na loaded po talaga sa asukal at flavorings,

4358
03:31:10,540 --> 03:31:13,180
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: baka po po pwedeng stick na lang ng coffee.

4359
03:31:14,240 --> 03:31:19,540
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Baka mas marami pang mabibili kesa sa limang pakete ng 3-in-1.

4360
03:31:19,700 --> 03:31:22,980
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Baka po pwedeng isang dosena na ng stick ng coffee.

4361
03:31:23,380 --> 03:31:27,040
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Kasi at least yun totoong kape at hindi loaded sa asukal.

4362
03:31:27,040 --> 03:31:30,740
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Nakalagay rin po doon ay Ovaltine.

4363
03:31:31,660 --> 03:31:34,440
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: And maganda po yun para sa mga bata.

4364
03:31:34,680 --> 03:31:38,120
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Pero sana magkaroon ng mas nutritious na substitute.

4365
03:31:38,680 --> 03:31:43,220
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Kasi ang tinitingnan lang po natin ay hindi lang yung may pantawid gutom,

4366
03:31:43,660 --> 03:31:48,900
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: kundi sana nutritious din po ang laman ng ating pinamimigay.

4367
03:31:49,420 --> 03:31:51,880
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: So wala po akong masyadong reklamo, sir.

4368
03:31:53,320 --> 03:31:54,920
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Mabilis ang aksyon.

4369
03:31:55,920 --> 03:31:56,400
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Sustained.

4370
03:31:57,040 --> 03:31:59,920
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Masyado nga pong na-pamper yung mga LGUs.

4371
03:32:00,420 --> 03:32:03,840
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Kasi under your watch, ngayon lang namin naramdaman

4372
03:32:03,840 --> 03:32:08,080
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: na hindi na iisipin ng LGUs kung ano ang ipamimigay.

4373
03:32:08,260 --> 03:32:10,600
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Kasi sustained siya.

4374
03:32:10,720 --> 03:32:15,120
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Hindi lang siya quick response, pero sustained ang response.

4375
03:32:15,340 --> 03:32:18,660
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Tuloy, yung probinsya ng Albay, for instance,

4376
03:32:19,240 --> 03:32:21,680
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: once lang namihagi ng bigas.

4377
03:32:21,680 --> 03:32:26,120
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: At nung pag-decamp, doon nagbigay pa ng fresh food.

4378
03:32:27,040 --> 03:32:32,240
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Yung mga LGUs naman po ay hindi na gumagamit ng kanilang quick response funds.

4379
03:32:32,600 --> 03:32:35,700
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Kasi umasa na lahat sa DSWD.

4380
03:32:36,280 --> 03:32:41,980
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: So kanina sinabi ninyo na kayo ang pang-augment.

4381
03:32:42,480 --> 03:32:44,280
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Hindi po ganun ang nangyayari.

4382
03:32:44,480 --> 03:32:47,940
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: So palagay ko may mali rin po doon sa senaryo, sir.

4383
03:32:49,500 --> 03:32:52,200
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Kailangan ata mapag-aralan din mabuti.

4384
03:32:52,480 --> 03:32:54,440
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: O mag-guide yung LGU.

4385
03:32:54,440 --> 03:32:56,260
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Kapag hindi ka nagbigay,

4386
03:32:57,040 --> 03:33:00,340
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: hindi ba po pwedeng i-ask sa lahat sa DSWD?

4387
03:33:01,060 --> 03:33:05,020
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Lahat ako, salita, hindi ko malang narinig yung response ninyo.

4388
03:33:05,220 --> 03:33:07,200
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: So again, maraming salamat po.

4389
03:33:07,520 --> 03:33:09,400
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Mr. Chairman, totally agree.

4390
03:33:10,360 --> 03:33:12,140
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Una ho yung efficiency.

4391
03:33:12,980 --> 03:33:17,380
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Now is the time that we study our options on individuals versus family packs.

4392
03:33:18,560 --> 03:33:22,220
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Mahirap sa logistics sa storekeeping, pero we're up to the challenge.

4393
03:33:22,980 --> 03:33:24,180
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Number two, variety.

4394
03:33:24,180 --> 03:33:26,820
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Hindi na lang ngayon kasi sa Albay nangyayari.

4395
03:33:27,040 --> 03:33:32,220
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Ito yung protracted disasters, like what we're seeing now in Central Luzon na one month and a half na.

4396
03:33:32,220 --> 03:33:38,940
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: When those boxes na, we just kept what it was nung na nakuha namin yung control ng department.

4397
03:33:38,940 --> 03:33:44,420
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Tama ko kayo, we have to start thinking of the new type of disasters that's hitting us.

4398
03:33:44,420 --> 03:33:46,420
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And variety is something that's important.

4399
03:33:46,420 --> 03:33:48,820
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The food fatigue is something that's real.

4400
03:33:48,820 --> 03:33:50,820
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: At kaya kami nakakarinig rin.

4401
03:33:50,820 --> 03:33:52,820
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So we will take that into account.

4402
03:33:52,820 --> 03:33:56,860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: But the first two items, well noted, we will study.

4403
03:33:56,860 --> 03:33:58,860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Mahirap kasi ho.

4404
03:33:58,860 --> 03:34:02,860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: That means us storekeeping multiple types of packs.

4405
03:34:02,860 --> 03:34:04,860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: But we're up to the challenge.

4406
03:34:04,860 --> 03:34:08,860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Number three, yung 3-1 coffee.

4407
03:34:08,860 --> 03:34:10,860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Ako, I myself drink black and I agree.

4408
03:34:10,860 --> 03:34:15,860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Pero gusto ko lang ko i-point out, lahat ho yun, bago nalagay sa kahon, dumadaan sa FNRI.

4409
03:34:15,860 --> 03:34:19,860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: It passed their minimum standards, but we will review.

4410
03:34:19,860 --> 03:34:21,860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Well noted as well, Madam Chair.

4411
03:34:21,860 --> 03:34:24,860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Mr. Chair, and last but not the least, yun sa QRF.

4412
03:34:24,860 --> 03:34:25,860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Ma'am, you read my mind.

4413
03:34:25,860 --> 03:34:30,860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And you said what I can't say publicly because we're in the middle of a disaster.

4414
03:34:30,860 --> 03:34:38,860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: But rest assured that we're already talking to DBM because we're seeing slow or low utilization ng mga quick response sa LGU level.

4415
03:34:38,860 --> 03:34:46,860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And I would also point out nga na unlike the national QRF na na-exhaust sa lokal, you know this very well,

4416
03:34:46,860 --> 03:34:50,860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: nare-revert yan after two years or three years into the general fund.

4417
03:34:50,860 --> 03:34:52,860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Five years pala, sorry, five years.

4418
03:34:52,860 --> 03:34:55,860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: I haven't practiced local government in more than four years now.

4419
03:34:55,860 --> 03:35:00,860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So we have to really think about what you said.

4420
03:35:00,860 --> 03:35:03,860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Kasi ang sinasabi nyo, lagi ko rin yan sinasabi na sa isip ko.

4421
03:35:03,860 --> 03:35:08,860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Pero we're going to find a way to make the LGUs counterpart man lang.

4422
03:35:08,860 --> 03:35:11,860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Kasi nga, like I said, mabigat na ng pabigat.

4423
03:35:11,860 --> 03:35:22,860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And I hope we see lang kasi the only reason why we're doing this massive is because in a hungry family, walang national government, walang local government.

4424
03:35:22,860 --> 03:35:24,860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Pag galit siya sa gobyerno, galit siya sa gobyerno.

4425
03:35:24,860 --> 03:35:26,860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Kung hindi siya nakakuha ng pagkain, galit siya.

4426
03:35:26,860 --> 03:35:34,860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Pero it's no reason for the lopsided utilization of the QRF.

4427
03:35:34,860 --> 03:35:39,860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: While the national government is using its QRF massively to a point na nade-deplete natin,

4428
03:35:39,860 --> 03:35:47,860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: the local government will look at how they utilize and how to prod them with the help of DILG and DBM to spend their QRFs also.

4429
03:35:47,860 --> 03:35:53,860
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: I would just like to add na maganda yung aksyon na ginawa ng DSWD

4430
03:35:54,860 --> 03:36:04,860
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: na nagbigay ng Emergency Cash Assistance para mabibili nila yung mga [unclear] items na kailangan rin nila.

4431
03:36:04,860 --> 03:36:12,860
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Pero sa 7 buwan at isang Emergency Cash Assistance, baka sa susunod pa pwedeng planuhin na mas madalas.

4432
03:36:12,860 --> 03:36:17,860
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: May cash for work. One cash for work, one emergency cash assistance.

4433
03:36:17,860 --> 03:36:22,860
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: So baka mas tingnan natin kung pa paano mabalansihin.

4434
03:36:22,860 --> 03:36:28,880
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And since it's an ongoing disaster, si Mayon hasn't really de-escalated.

4435
03:36:29,400 --> 03:36:33,940
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The Undersecretary for Disaster will sit down with a good Congresswoman on packaging more.

4436
03:36:34,300 --> 03:36:38,300
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: But well noted not just for Mayon but for every other protracted disaster.

4437
03:36:39,960 --> 03:36:44,000
Rep. Cielo Krisel Lagman: Maraming maraming salamat, Secretary. And congratulations, job well done.

4438
03:36:46,200 --> 03:36:48,160
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Thank you, Kong Lagman.

4439
03:36:48,840 --> 03:36:51,880
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: As if we're running out of interpellators, Mr. Secretary.

4440
03:36:51,880 --> 03:36:57,980
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: The good thing is we have with us the Committee Chair of the Ways and Means.

4441
03:36:58,400 --> 03:37:03,960
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: We recognize Congressman Miro Quimbo.

4442
03:37:05,100 --> 03:37:06,480
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Thank you very much.

4443
03:37:06,920 --> 03:37:13,280
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Actually, I wasn't supposed to ask you a question, but it seems that for the first time we're running out of warm bodies.

4444
03:37:13,280 --> 03:37:21,860
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: So just to keep the conversation going, well, I mean honestly, I have nothing to ask.

4445
03:37:21,980 --> 03:37:26,500
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Because how do you fix something that's already working?

4446
03:37:28,800 --> 03:37:32,480
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: I think we have very hardworking employees.

4447
03:37:34,060 --> 03:37:36,800
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: The response time has become so much quicker.

4448
03:37:38,220 --> 03:37:47,740
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Even in terms of professionalizing the distribution and pickup of our pag-asa boxes.

4449
03:37:48,100 --> 03:37:49,480
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: How do we call our boxes again?

4450
03:37:49,620 --> 03:37:50,580
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Family food box.

4451
03:37:50,700 --> 03:37:51,700
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Family food box.

4452
03:37:51,880 --> 03:38:01,220
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: I said that earlier, in previous years, parang kahon ng pag-asa.

4453
03:38:01,680 --> 03:38:03,960
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Because it does. I mean, that's what it does.

4454
03:38:04,020 --> 03:38:13,260
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Meaning when people see it, it's already a symbol of something that addresses deep wants at a very dire moment.

4455
03:38:13,920 --> 03:38:18,020
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: So tingin ko, baka pag-isipan natin, it's too businesslike.

4456
03:38:18,020 --> 03:38:20,960
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: It's too Rex Gatchal yan.

4457
03:38:21,880 --> 03:38:27,520
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Parang it's part of a key performance indicator.

4458
03:38:28,000 --> 03:38:29,320
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Parang ganun ang dating eh, di ba?

4459
03:38:29,960 --> 03:38:31,100
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: What's it called? Family?

4460
03:38:31,340 --> 03:38:32,320
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Family food pack.

4461
03:38:33,480 --> 03:38:33,920
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: FFP.

4462
03:38:34,160 --> 03:38:35,000
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Palitan mo na yun.

4463
03:38:35,400 --> 03:38:36,440
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We will, Mr. Chair.

4464
03:38:37,000 --> 03:38:41,540
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: I think with something more, yeah, something more spiritual, di ba?

4465
03:38:41,560 --> 03:38:42,160
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Hopeful, yeah.

4466
03:38:42,220 --> 03:38:44,000
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Yeah, yung aspirational.

4467
03:38:44,000 --> 03:38:51,780
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: But anyway, so even the way that it's managed, the way they are packed, these are very simple things.

4468
03:38:51,880 --> 03:38:57,640
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: But even on the part of the end user, you see them very much satisfied.

4469
03:38:57,640 --> 03:39:05,440
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: And even the way it is packed today, I have rarely heard of anyone actually na, ang tawag dyan, binuburiki eh.

4470
03:39:06,160 --> 03:39:11,580
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Yung dinidismantle and then nilalagay in their own political packaging.

4471
03:39:12,120 --> 03:39:13,600
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Hindi ko na rin nababalitaan yan eh.

4472
03:39:13,900 --> 03:39:16,580
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Kasi sobrang hirap yata i-unbundle.

4473
03:39:16,760 --> 03:39:18,560
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Tanggal pala yung scotch tape dyan, di ba?

4474
03:39:19,160 --> 03:39:21,360
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: So, but like I said,

4475
03:39:21,880 --> 03:39:25,680
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: yung tanong ko na lang is really on senior citizen pension.

4476
03:39:26,680 --> 03:39:34,440
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: So, I've seen that while the budget for this, for next year, is actually lower, slightly lower from this year.

4477
03:39:34,440 --> 03:39:43,400
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Despite the fact that the target has increased by, I think, more than 50,000, ang additional beneficiaries.

4478
03:39:43,920 --> 03:39:45,840
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Pero bakit mas mababa yung budget?

4479
03:39:47,440 --> 03:39:49,380
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Mr. Chairman, ano kasi yun?

4480
03:39:50,160 --> 03:39:51,720
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Congressional amendment?

4481
03:39:51,880 --> 03:39:52,880
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Yung nadagdag?

4482
03:39:53,380 --> 03:39:55,420
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And even that, kasi kapos na kapos eh.

4483
03:39:55,540 --> 03:40:01,060
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We are fully supportive of the provision that you've been pushing together with former Congresswoman Stella

4484
03:40:01,060 --> 03:40:06,180
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: on a universal senior pension, social pension for senior citizens.

4485
03:40:06,800 --> 03:40:09,980
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: It will address the public perception na pinipili.

4486
03:40:10,740 --> 03:40:11,960
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And we totally agree.

4487
03:40:12,140 --> 03:40:16,500
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Sana hawa, huwag lang ma-restore, but we add more to cater to all of them.

4488
03:40:17,440 --> 03:40:21,500
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Yeah, I think, Chairman, the point here relative to senior citizens,

4489
03:40:21,880 --> 03:40:26,880
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: and pension is, nothing can be worse when you're doing a great program,

4490
03:40:27,060 --> 03:40:29,720
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: but you receive more criticisms than praises.

4491
03:40:30,240 --> 03:40:34,400
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Because yung tumatanggap, kadalasan di naman nagpapasalamat na eh, diba?

4492
03:40:35,460 --> 03:40:40,100
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Pero yung hindi nakakatanggap na karamihan, ay yun ang pinuputakti tayo.

4493
03:40:40,460 --> 03:40:42,520
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Actually, Mr. Chairman, tama ho yun. Plus minus eh.

4494
03:40:42,640 --> 03:40:44,380
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Kasi mas malaki yung minus than yung plus.

4495
03:40:44,480 --> 03:40:49,300
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Kasi at the running rate of 11 million senior citizens, and we're only catering to 4.5 to 5,

4496
03:40:49,300 --> 03:40:51,860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: that means yung 6 na milyon na hindi nakakatanggap,

4497
03:40:51,880 --> 03:40:55,160
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: minus dun sa lamang pahuyong hindi nakatanggap na galit.

4498
03:40:55,880 --> 03:40:59,060
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: At saka, ayoko naman lahat eh, pero marami sa ating mga kababayan,

4499
03:40:59,500 --> 03:41:01,220
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: katatanggap pa lang ng benepisyo,

4500
03:41:01,760 --> 03:41:06,880
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: ang susunod ay imbis sa magsabi ng maraming salamat sa Pangulo, sa DSWD,

4501
03:41:07,920 --> 03:41:10,880
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: ang kadalasan nadidinig ko eh, ano pa kaya susunod?

4502
03:41:11,880 --> 03:41:16,400
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Diba? So, I really think that the program needs to be expanded.

4503
03:41:16,400 --> 03:41:21,680
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: So, there's an existing proposal here to have a reduced,

4504
03:41:21,880 --> 03:41:26,180
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: ah, amount for the new ones, meaning instead of 1,000 a month,

4505
03:41:26,740 --> 03:41:29,940
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: 500 pesos a month lang so that the outlay becomes half.

4506
03:41:30,400 --> 03:41:34,700
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: And I think it's going to be more palatable and obviously it's going to be more affordable.

4507
03:41:35,460 --> 03:41:41,100
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Sabi ko nga, Sek, imbis na dinadala sa kung ano-ano flood control, dito lang natin dalhin.

4508
03:41:41,480 --> 03:41:43,480
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Kasi dito mas napapakinabangan pa ng tao.

4509
03:41:43,920 --> 03:41:48,480
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Mr. Chairman, we agree 101% on both counts.

4510
03:41:49,560 --> 03:41:50,940
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Half, but everybody.

4511
03:41:50,940 --> 03:41:56,660
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And at the same time, yun nga, we put our money where we know na talagang direkto sa tao.

4512
03:41:56,940 --> 03:41:58,700
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Huwag lang magalit ko si Sekvin sa akin.

4513
03:41:59,160 --> 03:42:01,340
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Kasi that means a minus to his side.

4514
03:42:02,100 --> 03:42:09,420
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Yeah, at the appropriate time, Mr. Chairman, we will move that more funding be given dito.

4515
03:42:09,620 --> 03:42:15,400
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Kasi, you know, it's so hard to explain to our SSS and GSIS pensioners,

4516
03:42:15,760 --> 03:42:20,340
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: especially our SS pensioners who only get a pension of, on the average,

4517
03:42:20,460 --> 03:42:20,920
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: between

4518
03:42:20,920 --> 03:42:22,040
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: three to five thousand a month.

4519
03:42:22,680 --> 03:42:27,560
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: So, ang tingin talaga nila is bakit kami paparasahan na nagsipag kami.

4520
03:42:27,900 --> 03:42:32,200
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: For lack of a better explanation, is ang tingin nila is kami nagtrabaho,

4521
03:42:32,340 --> 03:42:35,280
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: o yung asawa namin nagtrabaho, kaya may survivor pension kami,

4522
03:42:35,780 --> 03:42:37,860
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: but we are automatically disqualified.

4523
03:42:38,340 --> 03:42:44,440
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: While itong kapitbahay namin na buong buhay niya ay walang kinontribute sa economy in terms of livelihood,

4524
03:42:45,540 --> 03:42:50,880
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: siya ay nari-rewardan when the source of the funds really come from,

4525
03:42:50,920 --> 03:42:52,840
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: taxpayers, including themselves,

4526
03:42:53,000 --> 03:42:58,360
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: especially since they had been paying compensation taxes during their entire working life.

4527
03:42:58,620 --> 03:43:00,680
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: So, ang hirap i-justify, eh.

4528
03:43:00,780 --> 03:43:04,200
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: And I think nadidiminish yung ganda ng programa.

4529
03:43:05,160 --> 03:43:12,620
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Mr. Chair, we totally agree, and we're 101% behind that concept na huwag ipinalize yung mga may pension.

4530
03:43:13,440 --> 03:43:14,320
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And sang-ayon ho kami.

4531
03:43:15,360 --> 03:43:20,520
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: At sana, Secretary, is we really move towards,

4532
03:43:20,920 --> 03:43:25,140
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: a more contactless electronic transfer.

4533
03:43:25,800 --> 03:43:29,900
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Kasi, kawawa rin yung ating mga beneficiaries, kailangan pa i-biyahe,

4534
03:43:30,340 --> 03:43:31,820
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: especially mga senior citizens.

4535
03:43:32,580 --> 03:43:37,140
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: At wala naman akong pinapatunguhan o pinaparinggan,

4536
03:43:37,280 --> 03:43:40,760
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: pero gusto-gusto na ibang mga politiko na iniipon, eh.

4537
03:43:41,260 --> 03:43:45,300
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Di ba, iniipon, magtatagal yung mga ating mga lolo't lola,

4538
03:43:45,840 --> 03:43:50,020
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: at nakikita mo, talagang they will have to hire tricycles to get to the venue,

4539
03:43:50,120 --> 03:43:50,820
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: They have to pay 150 pesos

4540
03:43:50,920 --> 03:43:54,260
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: one way, so 300 piso ka agad yun, di ba?

4541
03:43:54,400 --> 03:43:56,120
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: So, ang laking na ibabawas.

4542
03:43:57,680 --> 03:44:05,020
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Sabi ko nga is, we need to keep pushing towards an electronic, more seamless distribution system.

4543
03:44:05,940 --> 03:44:11,420
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Mr. Chairman, in fact, that move is already being done in the uplift assistance bucket 2.

4544
03:44:12,040 --> 03:44:16,380
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Kanina na talakay ho namin na we're working with the BSP on banking the unbanked,

4545
03:44:16,460 --> 03:44:17,140
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: lalo na sa mahirap.

4546
03:44:17,140 --> 03:44:19,860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We saw in UPLIFT bucket number two, yung poor at near poor.

4547
03:44:20,920 --> 03:44:23,800
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Yung poor, almost 80% are unbanked.

4548
03:44:24,240 --> 03:44:28,960
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: That's why what we did with the BSP is to get the banks and the e-wallets on site already.

4549
03:44:28,960 --> 03:44:39,380
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, pag-payout, nire-register na rin namin with the hopes of banking that 2.5 million na mga Pilipino na mahihirap at near poor na walang banko.

4550
03:44:39,440 --> 03:44:40,840
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: But we totally agree, Mr. Chairman.

4551
03:44:42,080 --> 03:44:45,380
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: I just hope that it will not also lead to delay, no?

4552
03:44:45,540 --> 03:44:50,640
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Yung while there will be birth pains, meaning registration,

4553
03:44:50,920 --> 03:44:55,920
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: that will take time, but after that, baka pwedeng seamless na talaga.

4554
03:44:56,040 --> 03:44:59,320
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: They get it from Cebuana or they get it from their own.

4555
03:45:00,000 --> 03:45:01,650
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: electronic wallets.

4556
03:45:01,650 --> 03:45:11,280
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Mr. Chair, we're gradually growing the database ng poor na walang banko, na walang bank. Yun nga yung sa UPLIFT bucket number two

4557
03:45:11,280 --> 03:45:16,720
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: with the hopes na on the third tranche, kasi napakaliit lang ho yung may bank account sa first tranche eh.

4558
03:45:16,720 --> 03:45:22,400
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So hopefully lahat ng mga napapasok namin digital na sila, pero we need to grow it talaga.

4559
03:45:22,400 --> 03:45:24,630
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Malayo pa ho tayo doon sa may mga bank accounts.

4560
03:45:24,630 --> 03:45:29,790
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Okay, now that there are other warm bodies, I think it's time for me to wrap up.

